  "goodToKnow": "Der Jakobsweg is the Way of St James, the pilgrimage route to Santiago de Compostela in Spain, marked by a scallop shell (Jakobsmuschel). Many Jakobswege also cross Germany. Comedian Hape Kerkeling's 2006 book Ich bin dann mal weg, about his walk, became a huge bestseller and sent many Germans on the Camino. Plural: die Jakobswege."
